{
  "id": "28907_togaraseru",
  "headword": "{尖|とが}らせる",
  "reading": "とがらせる",
  "romaji": "togaraseru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (ichidan)",
  "gloss": "to sharpen; to point; to purse (lips)",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to sharpen; to make pointed; to purse (lips)",
      "explanation": "To make something pointy at the tip. Also used figuratively with {口|くち} (mouth/lips) to mean pouting or sulking, and with {神経|しんけい} (nerves) to mean being on edge."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "28907_togaraseru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{鉛筆|えんぴつ}を{尖|とが}らせる。",
      "english": "To sharpen a pencil.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28907_togaraseru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{弟|おとうと}は{口|くち}を{尖|とが}らせて{文句|もんく}を{言|い}った。",
      "english": "My little brother pursed his lips and complained.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28907_togaraseru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{試合|しあい}{前|まえ}の{選手|せんしゅ}たちは{神経|しんけい}を{尖|とが}らせていた。",
      "english": "The players were on edge before the match.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The transitive/causative form of {尖|とが}る (to become pointed).\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nTransitive (takes を). Pairs with intransitive {尖|とが}る.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {鉛筆|えんぴつ}を{尖|とが}らせる: to sharpen a pencil\n- {口|くち}を{尖|とが}らせる: to pout; to purse one's lips (in displeasure)\n- {神経|しんけい}を{尖|とが}らせる: to be on edge; to be highly alert\n- {耳|みみ}を{尖|とが}らせる: to listen sharply\n\nUSAGE:\n{口|くち}を{尖|とが}らせる is the standard way to describe a sulky or complaining facial expression. {神経|しんけい}を{尖|とが}らせる describes heightened sensitivity or vigilance, often about a specific issue.",
